# Which films won eleven Oscars?
subtitle: "Tap the three films that share the record of eleven Oscars, and find out which one won every award it was up for."

## Which films won eleven Oscars?
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: ampas
      title: Academy Awards database
      authors: Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences
      year: 2025
      finding: 'Ben-Hur (1959, 11 of 12 nominations), Titanic (1997, 11 of 14) and The Lord of the Rings: The Return of the King (2003, 11 of 11) each won 11 Oscars; West Side Story (1961) won 10; Casablanca, The Godfather and Avatar 3 each'

    cards films cites ["ampas"] x 20 width 960 select "Won 11" hidden true
        * "Ben-Hur" icon.of horse icon.set twemoji in true
        * "Titanic" icon.of ship icon.set twemoji in true
        * "Return of the King" icon.of ring icon.set twemoji in true
        * "West Side Story" icon.of "woman dancing" icon.set twemoji in false
        * "The Godfather" icon.of rose icon.set twemoji in false
        * "Avatar" icon.of alien icon.set twemoji in false
        * "Casablanca" icon.of airplane icon.set twemoji in false
    text l_ben "1959 · 11/12" #2f6b8f x 215 y 245 font_size 26 hidden true
    text l_tit "1997 · 11/14" #2f6b8f x 405 y 245 font_size 26 hidden true
    text l_rotk "2003 · 11/11" #b5482e x 595 y 245 font_size 28 hidden true
    icon trophy size 130 set twemoji x 830 y 300 icon_look picture of trophy hidden true

    card title "Which films won 11 Oscars?"

The record for Oscars won by a single film is eleven, and only a handful of films have reached it.
    draw films

    ask "Which of these films won eleven Oscars? Tap every one." on films store f feedback.style warm feedback.perfect "You could host the ceremony." feedback.good "A seasoned film buff." feedback.poor "The epics blur together for most of us." feedback.none "Hollywood fooled you this time."
        right: All {f.total} right.
        wrong: {f} of {f.total} on the first try.

Three films share the record. Ben-Hur came first, in 1959, chariot race and all.
    draw l_ben

Titanic matched it in 1997, from fourteen nominations.
    draw l_tit

West Side Story came painfully close, with ten.
    text l_wss "← 10" #2f6b8f x 300 y 511 font_size 40

But the third, The Lord of the Rings: The Return of the King, did something the others did not.
    draw l_rotk

It won every single award it was nominated for: eleven out of eleven.
    draw trophy

And it was the first fantasy film ever to win Best Picture.
    point at.ref l_rotk gesture underline

