audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    '|a||Which films won eleven Oscars?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
    '|a||Tap the three films that share the record of eleven Oscars, and find out which one won every award it was up for.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
    '|a||The record for Oscars won by a single film is eleven, and only a handful of films have reached it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
    '|a||Which of these films won eleven Oscars? Tap every one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
    '|a||Three films share the record. Ben-Hur came first, in 1959, chariot race and all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
    '|a||Titanic matched it in 1997, from fourteen nominations.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
    '|a||West Side Story came painfully close, with ten.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
    '|a||But the third, The Lord of the Rings: The Return of the King, did something the others did not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
    '|a||It won every single award it was nominated for: eleven out of eleven.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
    '|a||And it was the first fantasy film ever to win Best Picture.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 0
      voice: en-US-Studio-Q
